title: Work the institutions
new-page: true

= Work the institutions

The Left cannot govern from 49 seats. It can still decide which relationships,
constitutional principles and future coalitions survive the coming crisis.

- @ko
- @psl
- @duda
- @courts
- @pis_social
- @poland_hub: Spend no action

@ko
title: Establish a permanent working channel with KO
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Useful now; dangerous to Left independence.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; month_actions += 1; ko_relation += 8 if ko_coalition_openness >= 50; ko_relation += 4 if ko_coalition_openness < 50; public_trust += 1 if ko_coalition_openness >= 50; razem_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "The democratic opposition tests whether it can coordinate"

Joint parliamentary procedure reduces avoidable defeats. Razem warns that a
working channel can become silent subordination to the larger liberal party.

- @poland_hub: Return to the leadership table

@psl
title: Open a rural and social-policy channel with PSL
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Builds a hinge relationship at progressive cost.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; month_actions += 1; psl_relation += 9 if psl_coalition_openness >= 45; psl_relation += 4 if psl_coalition_openness < 45; local_network += 2; progressives_dissent += 4; spring_dissent += 2; psl_conservative_share += 1 if psl_coalition_openness < 45; news_headline = "PSL prices another month of coalition courtship"

The conversation begins with pensions, clinics and municipal finance—not
abortion or Church policy. PSL appreciates the order. Progressive organisers
recognise the future veto before anyone says the word.

- @poland_hub: Return to the leadership table

@duda
title: Prepare a bill-by-bill dossier for President Duda
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Improves Palace access without creating an alliance.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; month_actions += 1; president_relation += 7; constitutional_restraint += 2; barons_dissent -= 1; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The Palace accepts a policy briefing"

The approach is deliberately narrow: disability, pensions, labour inspection
and public health. One presidential signature will not settle abortion, media
or the courts, but it may prove that PiS does not own every decision.

- @poland_hub: Return to the leadership table

@courts
title: Defend judicial independence without promising a purge
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Legitimacy now; no instant personnel victory.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; month_actions += 1; judicial_legitimacy += 7; constitutional_restraint += 5; progressive_credibility += 2; president_relation -= 3; pis_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The Left publishes a lawful repair doctrine"

The doctrine separates the Tribunal, KRS, Supreme Court and prosecutors. It
promises individual review and continuity of ordinary judgments. Militants
find it slow; lawyers find it usable.

- @poland_hub: Return to the leadership table

@pis_social
title: Negotiate one social amendment with PiS
subtitle: No resource cost. Delivery, but high opposition and factional costs.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; pis_relation += 7 if pis_accept_social >= 50; pis_relation += 2 if pis_accept_social < 50; government_delivery += 3 if pis_accept_social >= 50; household_security += 3 if pis_accept_social >= 50; public_trust -= 2 if pis_accept_social < 50; ko_relation -= 5; razem_dissent += 4; progressives_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "A social amendment tests PiS's solidarist wing"

A social amendment passes with Left votes. Beneficiaries do not care who owned
the bill; KO does. Every caucus now asks whether an exception has become a
strategy.

- @poland_hub: Return to the leadership table
